[audio.c:405-433](../../nuttx/audio/audio.c#L405-L433) is the answer:

```c
for (priv = upper->head; priv != NULL; priv = priv->flink)
  {
    if (priv->state == AUDIO_STATE_OPEN || priv->state == AUDIO_STATE_PAUSED)
      continue;                    /* skipped -- never sets ready */
    ...
  }

if (!ready || ...)
  return OK;                       /* returns success, enqueues nothing */
```

A session still in `AUDIO_STATE_OPEN` is skipped, `ready` stays false, and `audio_try_enqueue` returns **OK without ever calling `lower->ops->enqueuebuffer`**. The enqueue is accepted and silently discarded.

My ordering enqueues all four record buffers *before* `AUDIOIOC_START`, so every one of them hit that path. Let me confirm what moves a session out of `AUDIO_STATE_OPEN`.

